 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hello! How's everything today?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.52,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_28"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty relaxed today.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.75,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How do they even get the caffeine out of decaf? Is it chemicals?",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.45,
   "block": "coffee.dlg23",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Sometimes, but not always. There are a few methods. One uses only water, soaking the green beans and filtering the caffeine out.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Wesley, tell me honestly, was that film rubbish or was it just me?",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.64,
   "block": "nq_social_021",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "other_name",
   "phrasing": "nq_social_021",
   "name_pos": "start",
   "addressee": "Wesley"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "other",
   "text": "It was rubbish. The ending made no sense.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.88,
   "block": "nq_social_021"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Only water? That's it?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.95,
   "block": "coffee.dlg23",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Water and a special carbon filter. Another method uses carbon dioxide under pressure. And some use solvents that are mostly removed afterwards.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.68,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Which one",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.62,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "coffee.dlg23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "tastes best?",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 2.92,
   "block": "coffee.dlg23",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Taste depends more on the beans and roasting, but many people like the water and carbon dioxide processed ones. The bag often says which method was used.",
   "est_sec": 8.47,
   "gap_before": 1.01,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I always thought decaf tasted like cardboard.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "block": "coffee.dlg23",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It used to, often. Good decaf today can be really delicious. Try one from a specialty roaster, you might be surprised.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 1.14,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "coffee.dlg23"
  }
 ]
